2026-09-12T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2247) 'Property testing in every language, with falsification
 # uuid: 25be7733-4fd7-55d3-8a8f-2066493f3561
 # tags: rfd:title
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-09-12T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2247) 'every test suite in the workspace states invariants a generator searches, and ships the negative control that must fail
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2247) 'every language in the workspace: Elixir (StreamData), Python (Hypothesis), C++ (RapidCheck), Rust (proptest), Go (testing/quick, rapid), GDScript/C# (FsCheck where hosted)
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2247) 'Every test states an invariant a generator searches, with a control that must fail.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2247) 'Example-based tests pass by construction. The author picks inputs they already believe work, so the suite encodes the author's assumptions rather than testing them, and it goes green over a harness that measures nothing.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2247) 'Pair each new property with its negative control: the input that should violate it, with the test failing if the violation goes undetected. The sections below list the property shapes.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2247) 'Properties worth stating, and how falsification pairs with them
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2247) 'The useful properties are the ones that hold for every input rather than the ones convenient to write down. Below are the recurring shapes, each with the negative control that gives it teeth, drawn from work already in the workspace.
 # tags: rfd:details-preamble
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2247) 'A test asserts an invariant over generated input, not an outcome for one hand-chosen input. Every language the workspace builds in uses its property-testing library. On top of that, every property ships its falsification: the input that SHOULD violate it, with the test failing if the violation goes undetected.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2247) 'RFD66606-2234 (dress-on pipeline; the "every gate ships with its negative control" discipline this generalises, and the springbone follow-on whose harness bug motivated it), RFD66606-2232 (Markdown as build artifact), `2-contract/manuals-weftspun/apparatus/springbone_mujoco.py` and its test suite, `3-interactor/g1-sim-to-real/` (add_cloth_chains.py, bench_silhouette.py, coacd_calibrate.py).
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2247) 'Property shapes
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2247) '- **Monotonicity.** Raising a parameter moves the result one way. Raising spring-bone `pull` must not increase deflection; keeping every 4th bone must not score better than keeping every 2nd. Falsification: assert the comparison is strict where the model says it must be, so an implementation that ignores the parameter entirely fails instead of tying.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2247) '- **Conservation.** A transformation preserves a quantity it must not change. Merging parameter-identical springbone chains changes the component count and nothing else: transform count before equals after. Falsification: a merge that drops a transform must fail the test.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2247) '- **Round-trip identity.** Export then import returns the input. The engine's USD adapter carried blend shapes out and silently dropped every one on the way back in, because no test round-tripped a mesh that had any. Falsification: perturb one shape's deltas and assert the round trip detects the difference, so an importer returning the ORIGINAL mesh unchanged cannot pass.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2247) '- **Invariance.** An irrelevant change does not alter the result. Arclength-resampling a curve is invariant to how finely it was discretised. Falsification: a genuinely different curve must NOT compare equal, or the metric has flattened everything to zero and approves any reduction.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2247) '- **Ordering and idempotence.** Applying a reduction twice equals applying it once; grouping is independent of input order.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2247) 'Pin regressions as explicit examples on top of the generator (Hypothesis `@example`, proptest's `.regressions` file). The generator finds the class; the pinned case proves the specific bug stays dead.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2247) 'The harness bug that motivated this
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2247) 'The springbone chain-reduction harness reported a tidy set of numbers: 61 spring-bone components reduced to 19, collision checks 1233 to 512. Twelve example-based tests passed.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2247) 'Two negative controls (a frozen chain that must NOT register motion, and a stiff chain that must deflect less than a soft one) failed with the same number, 0.2017 m, for every parameter setting. The harness was measuring the carrier translating the chains rigidly, never their articulation: `qpos` written each step teleports the carrier and imparts no velocity, so nothing swung.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2247) 'The component result survived, being pure combinatorics on parameter identity with no simulation involved. The collision result did not, and it was biased toward over-pruning, because a chain that never swings never approaches a collider it would really have hit.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2247) 'The falsification cases caught it and the twelve examples did not. A generator would have caught it faster and smaller: "deflection is monotone in pull" is one property over generated parameters, and it shrinks to a minimal counterexample instead of needing a human to guess which two settings to compare. That is the argument for both halves of this rule.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2247) 'The workspace already believes half of it. RFD66606-2234's gates each read "every gate ships with its negative control". That discipline was written down for data gates and practised nowhere else; this RFD generalises it to code and adds the generator.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2247) 'Determinism
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2247) 'Anything touching a simulator, a GPU or a sampler fixes its seed, and the seed is part of the recorded failure. A property test that cannot reproduce its own counterexample is a flake generator. MuJoCo, CoACD and EditScore runs all fall under this.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2247) 'What this does not ask for
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2247) 'Not every test becomes a property test. Wiring checks (does this menu item exist, does this file parse) stay as examples; there is no invariant to generalise. The rule binds where there is a claim about behaviour over a domain of inputs, which is where the interesting bugs are.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2247) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-12T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2247) 'A property without a negative control is barely better: it establishes that the assertion is reachable, not that it discriminates.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2247  1 LINE
 Text:Written
